1
00:00:01,969 --> 00:00:03,096
JIM: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:04,750
ED: <i>You have five
minutes, quiz kids.</i>

3
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:10,434
Wayne Enterprises runs Indian
Hill, but who runs Wayne Enterprises?

4
00:00:10,711 --> 00:00:12,907
FRANK: <i>A weapon is en
route to destroy the city.</i>

5
00:00:13,247 --> 00:00:17,412
I can't take on Nygma and Barbara
and the rest of them by myself.

6
00:00:17,584 --> 00:00:18,895
You said you want
to build an army, right?

7
00:00:18,919 --> 00:00:21,320
What about an army of freaks?

8
00:00:21,622 --> 00:00:22,954
Who ordered the
hit on my father?

9
00:00:23,123 --> 00:00:24,989
Frank Gordon. Your uncle.

10
00:00:25,158 --> 00:00:26,717
You have the right
to remain silent.

11
00:00:26,927 --> 00:00:28,896
(GRUNTS)

12
00:00:29,496 --> 00:00:32,295
Dock 9C. It's where the
weapon will be arriving.

13
00:00:32,533 --> 00:00:34,502
Jim. Do I hear a
favor coming on?

14
00:00:34,735 --> 00:00:39,036
- (MAN GRUNTING)
- What is coming into Dock 9C?

15
00:00:39,206 --> 00:00:42,301
Now I know who I
am. I'm The Riddler.

16
00:00:43,143 --> 00:00:44,183
It's good to see you, too.

17
00:00:44,444 --> 00:00:45,605
How'd things go with Selina?

18
00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:48,372
This is what I was made for.

19
00:00:48,582 --> 00:00:49,845
The clone is in place.

20
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:51,280
Good evening, Alfred.

21
00:00:51,919 --> 00:00:52,919
And to you, Master Bruce.

22
00:00:53,086 --> 00:00:54,831
FRANK: <i>You need to join
The Court of Owls, Jim.</i>

23
00:00:54,855 --> 00:00:56,551
A woman named
Kathryn is going to call.

24
00:00:56,723 --> 00:00:58,214
<i>He would have
been so proud of you.</i>

25
00:00:58,392 --> 00:01:00,384
No! (GASPS)

26
00:01:01,628 --> 00:01:02,628
Kathryn, I presume.

27
00:01:02,863 --> 00:01:03,922
<i>I killed my uncle.</i>

28
00:01:04,131 --> 00:01:05,463
<i>I make no apologies for it.</i>

29
00:01:05,699 --> 00:01:06,699
<i>Maybe it's time we meet.</i>

30
00:01:06,934 --> 00:01:08,425
KATHRYN: <i>My thought exactly.</i>

31
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:13,271
(WIND HOWLING)

32
00:01:34,161 --> 00:01:36,187
(BOTH PANTING)

33
00:01:37,364 --> 00:01:38,491
Hello?

34
00:01:39,399 --> 00:01:40,526
<i>Anyone home?</i>

35
00:01:40,867 --> 00:01:43,530
When this guy gets home, we
gotta ask him to kick on the heat.

36
00:01:43,804 --> 00:01:46,000
It's colder in here
than it is out there.

37
00:01:50,077 --> 00:01:51,511
Fascinating.

38
00:01:51,845 --> 00:01:54,474
I know you're hell-bent on
getting revenge on Nygma and all.

39
00:01:54,648 --> 00:01:56,549
And forming an army
of freaks is a great plan.

40
00:01:56,717 --> 00:01:59,551
- I mean, it was my idea, but...
- (SHUSHING)

41
00:01:59,987 --> 00:02:01,216
Quiet.

42
00:02:01,688 --> 00:02:02,747
I think I hear something.

43
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:04,689
Do you think it's him?

44
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:11,526
(GASPS)

45
00:02:15,235 --> 00:02:16,760
Mr. Fries.

46
00:02:19,006 --> 00:02:20,006
Welcome home.

47
00:02:20,273 --> 00:02:22,538
(GROANING)

48
00:02:24,378 --> 00:02:27,871
I see you still hold me responsible
for all of that awful monster rhetoric

49
00:02:28,081 --> 00:02:29,201
I spewed during my campaign.

50
00:02:29,282 --> 00:02:31,274
You ran people like
me out of Gotham.

51
00:02:31,885 --> 00:02:33,365
We both know I
only said those things

52
00:02:33,487 --> 00:02:35,287
because that's what the
voters wanted to hear.

53
00:02:38,058 --> 00:02:39,890
Your experiments, Mr. Fries...

54
00:02:40,761 --> 00:02:42,801
You're trying to reverse
your condition, aren't you?

55
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:44,498
I can help you.

56
00:02:45,265 --> 00:02:46,265
Why would you do that?

57
00:02:46,433 --> 00:02:48,595
My enemies took
everything from me.

58
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:50,760
Tried to murder me.

59
00:02:51,505 --> 00:02:53,337
You help me get my revenge,

60
00:02:53,674 --> 00:02:56,474
and when I take back my throne, I
will give you every resource you need

61
00:02:56,543 --> 00:02:58,375
to free yourself
from this icy prison.

62
00:03:02,382 --> 00:03:03,748
Even if I wanted to say yes,

63
00:03:03,917 --> 00:03:07,513
I can only survive a few hours
outside the cold without my suit.

64
00:03:08,822 --> 00:03:10,120
And you don't have it

65
00:03:10,357 --> 00:03:13,259
because it's been locked away
in a Wayne Enterprises black site

66
00:03:13,460 --> 00:03:15,258
ever since you
escaped Indian Hill.

67
00:03:17,497 --> 00:03:19,090
- Ivy?
- Oh.

68
00:03:22,536 --> 00:03:23,536
COBBLEPOT: <i>Ta-da.</i>

69
00:03:23,704 --> 00:03:24,704
MR. FREEZE: <i>My suit?</i>

70
00:03:31,078 --> 00:03:32,808
So, Mr. Fries...

71
00:03:34,047 --> 00:03:35,879
Will you join us?

72
00:03:39,352 --> 00:03:41,344
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

73
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:52,323
JIM: Where are we?

74
00:03:52,499 --> 00:03:54,900
KATHRYN: Where we
are is not important, James.

75
00:03:56,103 --> 00:03:58,402
What matters is why you're here.

76
00:03:58,972 --> 00:04:01,567
- You know why I killed my uncle.
- Yes, I do.

77
00:04:02,576 --> 00:04:04,602
Frank murdered your father.

78
00:04:05,178 --> 00:04:09,240
What I need to know is if you
hold us accountable for his actions.

79
00:04:10,016 --> 00:04:11,575
Frank acted alone.

80
00:04:11,885 --> 00:04:13,820
He admitted as much to me.

81
00:04:14,421 --> 00:04:15,445
Good.

82
00:04:16,423 --> 00:04:17,721
Then we can proceed.

83
00:04:18,859 --> 00:04:22,261
The city needs you now
more than ever, James.

84
00:04:22,496 --> 00:04:24,727
There's turmoil ahead.

85
00:04:24,965 --> 00:04:28,231
<i>And good men like you are going
to be needed to hold it together.</i>

86
00:04:28,401 --> 00:04:29,994
<i>But make no mistake,</i>

87
00:04:30,203 --> 00:04:34,470
The Court, and The Court
alone, can save Gotham.

88
00:04:35,709 --> 00:04:36,938
So what do you want me to do?

89
00:04:37,477 --> 00:04:39,810
Prove your loyalty to The Court.

90
00:04:41,348 --> 00:04:43,010
Killing my uncle wasn't enough?

91
00:04:43,183 --> 00:04:44,811
That was between you and Frank.

92
00:04:44,985 --> 00:04:46,817
It had nothing to do with us.

93
00:04:48,622 --> 00:04:50,921
When the time is right,
we will call upon you.

94
00:04:52,559 --> 00:04:54,721
And Frank's body? It's
still in the brownstone.

95
00:04:55,162 --> 00:04:57,063
We've already taken care of it.

96
00:04:58,365 --> 00:05:00,357
(INDISTINCT POLICE
RADIO CHATTER)

97
00:05:00,667 --> 00:05:03,603
- Who's the stiff?
- Jim's uncle, Frank Gordon.

98
00:05:04,371 --> 00:05:06,203
- Never met him.
- They were estranged.

99
00:05:06,473 --> 00:05:07,805
Have you seen Jim?

100
00:05:08,108 --> 00:05:09,440
He's working a case.

101
00:05:09,776 --> 00:05:12,211
Or he's walking in
the door as we speak.

102
00:05:12,379 --> 00:05:15,543
Hey, Jim. Come in. We, uh,
have some bad news for you.

103
00:05:16,850 --> 00:05:18,910
- What's going on?
- I'm sorry.

104
00:05:19,452 --> 00:05:21,648
We found your uncle's
body this morning.

105
00:05:23,590 --> 00:05:26,059
He was pulled out of the
harbor. I did my prelim.

106
00:05:26,226 --> 00:05:28,746
The burns on his left temple
suggest he was shot at close range.

107
00:05:29,095 --> 00:05:30,563
<i>Lab is running ballistics.</i>

108
00:05:30,764 --> 00:05:32,289
You saw him at the
cemetery yesterday.

109
00:05:32,465 --> 00:05:34,491
He seemed on edge.
Did he say anything?

110
00:05:35,535 --> 00:05:38,562
No. He, uh, just stopped
by to pay his respects.

111
00:05:39,873 --> 00:05:41,068
We didn't talk much.

112
00:05:42,309 --> 00:05:44,039
Thanks, Lee. I'll
take it from here.

113
00:05:44,477 --> 00:05:45,757
That's it? That's your reaction?

114
00:05:46,713 --> 00:05:47,793
What do you want me to say?

115
00:05:49,683 --> 00:05:52,551
I know you. You're
hiding something.

116
00:05:52,752 --> 00:05:54,330
- You know something.
- BULLOCK: <i>Lee, come on.</i>

117
00:05:54,354 --> 00:05:55,720
The man just lost his uncle.

118
00:05:55,889 --> 00:05:57,790
Yeah, Harvey. You just
keep covering for him.

119
00:05:58,191 --> 00:05:59,454
My condolences.

120
00:06:03,496 --> 00:06:05,829
She's right. You do know
something, don't you?

121
00:06:06,933 --> 00:06:08,492
Uncle Frank shot himself.

122
00:06:09,102 --> 00:06:11,142
Said it was the only way
to get me inside The Court.

123
00:06:11,438 --> 00:06:13,907
- Did it work?
- I met with a woman named Kathryn.

124
00:06:14,808 --> 00:06:17,869
She says I have to prove
my loyalty to The Court first.

125
00:06:18,912 --> 00:06:21,245
Look, I see the need
for playing it cool.

126
00:06:21,648 --> 00:06:24,327
But right now, The Court's readying
a weapon that could destroy the city.

127
00:06:24,351 --> 00:06:27,014
We don't have time to sit on
our thumbs and do nothing.

128
00:06:27,187 --> 00:06:29,747
I don't like it any more than
you do, but if I push too hard,

129
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:32,483
we might blow the only
chance we have at stopping this.

130
00:06:32,959 --> 00:06:34,757
And Uncle Frank
will have died in vain.

131
00:06:34,928 --> 00:06:37,329
Okay. So what do we do now?

132
00:06:38,765 --> 00:06:41,166
Kathryn said to get back to
work. Keep up appearances.

133
00:06:41,568 --> 00:06:45,471
It shouldn't be too hard.
Look who resurfaced.

134
00:06:49,109 --> 00:06:50,543
BARBARA: Hello?

135
00:06:51,378 --> 00:06:52,778
Ed?

136
00:06:53,613 --> 00:06:55,047
It's Barbara.

137
00:06:55,348 --> 00:06:57,908
Your old friend you've
been blowing off.

138
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:03,822
I'll allow you to call me Ed
because we have history.

139
00:07:04,457 --> 00:07:05,789
But my name

140
00:07:08,361 --> 00:07:09,361
is The Riddler.

141
00:07:10,430 --> 00:07:11,762
So the headlines say.

142
00:07:11,965 --> 00:07:14,161
(CHUCKLES) Now,
why are you here?

143
00:07:15,168 --> 00:07:16,693
When Penguin was mayor,

144
00:07:16,870 --> 00:07:18,634
did he mention a
mysterious group?

145
00:07:19,205 --> 00:07:21,125
One that controlled the
levers of power in Gotham

146
00:07:21,341 --> 00:07:23,833
from the shadows
with total impunity?

147
00:07:24,244 --> 00:07:27,009
- No.
- See, I didn't claw my way to the top

148
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:29,342
only to find out there's
someone above me.

149
00:07:29,649 --> 00:07:31,584
I've been trying to
find out who they are,

150
00:07:31,818 --> 00:07:34,788
but no one in this town seems
to know anything about them.

151
00:07:35,288 --> 00:07:36,888
Then how is it that
you know about them?

152
00:07:37,724 --> 00:07:38,987
Jim Gordon put me on to them.

153
00:07:39,893 --> 00:07:42,226
And what is his
interest in all this?

154
00:07:42,429 --> 00:07:45,831
He didn't say, but he
did ask me to investigate

155
00:07:45,999 --> 00:07:50,061
a shipment coming
into Dock 9C yesterday.

156
00:07:50,337 --> 00:07:53,865
The Harbormaster was
protecting a crate from Indian Hill.

157
00:07:54,207 --> 00:07:55,971
- What was inside?
- I don't know.

158
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:57,486
Before I got a
chance to find out,

159
00:07:57,510 --> 00:08:00,480
some masked assassin
slaughtered half my men.

160
00:08:02,882 --> 00:08:04,510
What do you know?

161
00:08:04,884 --> 00:08:06,284
When I was at Indian Hill,

162
00:08:06,953 --> 00:08:11,152
Professor Strange hinted at
some powerful secret group,

163
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:13,259
but he didn't tell
me who they were.

164
00:08:14,995 --> 00:08:17,931
This is the one
riddle that got away.

165
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:24,228
I will get you the
answer you seek.

166
00:08:25,939 --> 00:08:27,931
But I will do it in my own way.

167
00:08:28,308 --> 00:08:30,937
You're going to make a big
production of this, aren't you?

168
00:08:31,644 --> 00:08:35,137
Only someone with power and connections
would have information on this group.

169
00:08:35,782 --> 00:08:38,251
I need to speak
with Gotham's elite.

170
00:08:38,852 --> 00:08:43,256
And nothing brings out the bourgeoisie
quite like opening night at the theater.

171
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:46,322
Where wilt thou lead me?

172
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:51,129
Speak, for I will go no further.

173
00:08:52,465 --> 00:08:55,697
(AUDIENCE MURMURING
INDISTINCTLY)

174
00:09:00,173 --> 00:09:02,142
I say, Ghost...

175
00:09:03,043 --> 00:09:09,074
Speak your business
or I shall go no further.

176
00:09:09,349 --> 00:09:13,719
ED: My business is not
with you, Prince of Denmark.

177
00:09:13,887 --> 00:09:15,879
But with your audience.

178
00:09:16,356 --> 00:09:18,154
(AUDIENCE MURMURING)

179
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:25,365
I've come to address you,

180
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,296
the ruling class of Gotham.

181
00:09:28,468 --> 00:09:32,064
You've kept a
secret for far too long.

182
00:09:32,272 --> 00:09:34,241
But tonight,

183
00:09:34,674 --> 00:09:39,442
I will kidnap and torture one
of you to expose the truth.

184
00:09:39,779 --> 00:09:42,840
So spread the word
to all your friends.

185
00:09:43,049 --> 00:09:46,247
The Riddler is coming.

186
00:09:47,821 --> 00:09:53,761
Also, I found your performance
to be wooden and unrealistic.

187
00:09:54,761 --> 00:09:56,821
- (GROANS)
- (AUDIENCE GASPS)

188
00:10:00,066 --> 00:10:02,228
And, scene.

189
00:10:20,920 --> 00:10:23,856
And that, my old
mucker, is checkmate.

190
00:10:28,595 --> 00:10:30,086
Good game, Alfred.

191
00:10:31,998 --> 00:10:33,638
You let me win, didn't
you, Master Bruce?

192
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,101
- No way, Alfred.
- No way, my foot.

193
00:10:37,437 --> 00:10:38,757
That's very
unlike you, isn't it?

194
00:10:39,672 --> 00:10:42,938
And to be honest, I mean, you haven't been
yourself these past few days, have you?

195
00:10:43,943 --> 00:10:45,287
I don't know what
you're talking about.

196
00:10:45,311 --> 00:10:47,940
I think you do know what
I'm talking about. So, come on.

197
00:10:52,185 --> 00:10:53,380
Out with it.

198
00:10:55,321 --> 00:10:56,983
The other day when I came home,

199
00:10:57,190 --> 00:10:58,710
you asked how things
were with Selina.

200
00:10:59,759 --> 00:11:01,399
<i>I made it sound like
things were hopeful.</i>

201
00:11:03,329 --> 00:11:04,388
I lied.

202
00:11:05,932 --> 00:11:07,867
She said she never
wanted to see me again.

203
00:11:08,801 --> 00:11:09,801
<i>I was embarrassed.</i>

204
00:11:10,370 --> 00:11:15,206
I was afraid you'd ask me
about seeing Selina, and I'd lie...

205
00:11:17,277 --> 00:11:18,687
I just didn't want
to talk about it.

206
00:11:18,711 --> 00:11:20,145
Well, I...

207
00:11:20,747 --> 00:11:22,579
I understand, Master B.

208
00:11:24,551 --> 00:11:26,349
And thank you very
much for being so candid.

209
00:11:28,855 --> 00:11:30,983
And I really wouldn't
worry about Ms. Kyle.

210
00:11:31,157 --> 00:11:35,595
You know, time has a way of
sorting these things out, doesn't it?

211
00:11:39,432 --> 00:11:41,272
Talking of which, I
should check on the dinner.

212
00:11:43,336 --> 00:11:44,998
- Alfred.
- Sir.

213
00:11:47,674 --> 00:11:48,674
Thank you.

214
00:11:51,144 --> 00:11:52,373
You're a good friend.

215
00:11:53,846 --> 00:11:55,178
Glad to hear it, sir.

216
00:12:17,804 --> 00:12:19,067
(CELL PHONE BEEPS)

217
00:12:19,872 --> 00:12:20,965
It's me.

218
00:12:21,941 --> 00:12:23,102
It's happening again.

219
00:12:24,544 --> 00:12:26,445
(INDISTINCT RADIO CHATTER)

220
00:12:26,913 --> 00:12:27,913
Hey.

221
00:12:29,115 --> 00:12:31,846
So, the audience has
been accounted for.

222
00:12:32,685 --> 00:12:33,812
(SIGHS) Is this Hamlet?

223
00:12:34,420 --> 00:12:36,355
I guess he wasn't meant to be.

224
00:12:37,857 --> 00:12:39,377
You crossed paths
with Nygma recently.

225
00:12:39,492 --> 00:12:41,688
Any idea what this secret
is he's talking about?

226
00:12:41,861 --> 00:12:43,159
No, I have no clue.

227
00:12:43,329 --> 00:12:44,763
My guess is he just made it up.

228
00:12:44,998 --> 00:12:46,830
Captain, we got the all-clear.

229
00:12:47,166 --> 00:12:48,166
All right.

230
00:13:04,851 --> 00:13:05,971
This is all that's in there.

231
00:13:12,292 --> 00:13:13,885
(CAMERA CLICKS IN BACKGROUND)

232
00:13:14,527 --> 00:13:16,359
It's a riddle. Shocker.

233
00:13:17,130 --> 00:13:20,294
Written in iambic pentameter.
Like a Shakespearean sonnet.

234
00:13:21,067 --> 00:13:23,559
"I am a man who
holds a high position

235
00:13:23,770 --> 00:13:26,001
"Who shows two faces
to all those he rules

236
00:13:26,506 --> 00:13:29,340
"A fraud, criminal and
sometime politician

237
00:13:30,009 --> 00:13:33,275
"Gotham, my
constituency of fools"

238
00:13:34,514 --> 00:13:37,882
A two-faced politician whose
constituency is Gotham.

239
00:13:38,051 --> 00:13:40,611
- The Mayor?
- Fraud. Criminal.

240
00:13:41,087 --> 00:13:44,489
Sounds like he's describing Penguin,
but that doesn't make any sense.

241
00:13:44,657 --> 00:13:47,183
Ed told Lucius
he killed Penguin.

242
00:13:47,427 --> 00:13:50,955
Aubrey James. He was recently
reinstated, and he's been mayor before.

243
00:13:51,331 --> 00:13:54,062
Sometime politician.
But why not just grab him?

244
00:13:54,233 --> 00:13:55,233
Why tell us in advance?

245
00:13:55,401 --> 00:13:58,447
Because Nygma wants to make a show
of it, and make us look bad in the process.

246
00:13:58,471 --> 00:14:00,599
Call the Mayor's Office.
Tell them we're on our way.

247
00:14:07,013 --> 00:14:09,881
We don't need Nygma for
anything. He should be dead by now.

248
00:14:10,149 --> 00:14:11,669
He's obsessed with
finding the answer.

249
00:14:11,851 --> 00:14:13,683
Which is an easy
solution for us.

250
00:14:13,853 --> 00:14:17,255
Once he does, we'll
get rid of him. I promise.

251
00:14:18,091 --> 00:14:20,185
And how's him causing a
scene at the theater help us?

252
00:14:20,827 --> 00:14:21,827
It doesn't.

253
00:14:23,129 --> 00:14:24,324
But it does help me more

254
00:14:24,630 --> 00:14:27,862
fully announce myself
on the Gotham stage,

255
00:14:28,601 --> 00:14:29,933
if you'll forgive the pun.

256
00:14:30,737 --> 00:14:33,502
You wanna become
famous? Try dying.

257
00:14:33,673 --> 00:14:36,609
- I can help you with that.
- Okay, that's enough.

258
00:14:38,211 --> 00:14:39,702
What actually is your plan?

259
00:14:41,314 --> 00:14:42,714
Kidnap Mayor James.

260
00:14:44,183 --> 00:14:46,277
The man ran this
place for 10 years.

261
00:14:46,586 --> 00:14:49,556
If anyone knows about this
mysterious group, he does.

262
00:14:49,722 --> 00:14:51,213
You could've just said that.

263
00:14:51,391 --> 00:14:53,326
I could've had him
here, being tortured.

264
00:14:54,127 --> 00:14:58,292
Okay, see, but first I had to tell
the GCPD what I was going to do.

265
00:14:58,998 --> 00:15:01,900
How else am I supposed to
properly embarrass them publicly?

266
00:15:02,068 --> 00:15:05,869
My crimes must live up to my
name and this is no exception.

267
00:15:06,305 --> 00:15:10,003
And what if the Mayor doesn't
know anything about this group, hmm?

268
00:15:10,510 --> 00:15:12,809
- What then?
- I have a plan B to smoke them out.

269
00:15:12,979 --> 00:15:17,007
But first, I need
something from you.

270
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:19,912
There's a biker bar on the
corner of Spaulding and 8th.

271
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:21,952
It's full of brawlers, lowlifes.

272
00:15:22,121 --> 00:15:27,719
I need a bomb to
detonate there tonight.

273
00:15:28,861 --> 00:15:30,090
I'll let you know when.

274
00:15:30,430 --> 00:15:33,332
So tell us, genius, how do
you plan to get Aubrey James

275
00:15:33,499 --> 00:15:35,730
now that you've told the
GCPD you're going after him?

276
00:15:35,902 --> 00:15:37,029
Oh, that's simple.

277
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:39,803
They're gonna bring him to me.

278
00:15:44,911 --> 00:15:47,311
You know how many crooked
politicians there are in this city?

279
00:15:47,647 --> 00:15:50,549
This riddle could be for anyone.
Oh, my gosh, this is delicious.

280
00:15:50,817 --> 00:15:54,515
All the same, Mr. Mayor, we'd like to
move you to a safe house, immediately.

281
00:15:55,321 --> 00:15:57,847
Did you not see the
muscle twins over there?

282
00:15:58,024 --> 00:15:59,822
I'm perfectly safe here.

283
00:15:59,992 --> 00:16:01,912
Besides, what's The Riddler
want with me, anyway?

284
00:16:01,994 --> 00:16:03,234
BULLOCK: <i>We're not really sure.</i>

285
00:16:03,396 --> 00:16:07,094
He did say something to the
crowd at the theater about a secret.

286
00:16:08,334 --> 00:16:09,893
My life's an open book.

287
00:16:12,505 --> 00:16:14,667
You feeling okay,
Mr. Mayor? You look a little...

288
00:16:14,841 --> 00:16:17,606
It's my blood sugar. I've had
too many of these danishes.

289
00:16:17,777 --> 00:16:19,109
Where are my pills?

290
00:16:19,879 --> 00:16:21,390
Wait a minute, where
did you get these?

291
00:16:21,414 --> 00:16:23,280
An appreciative citizen. Why?

292
00:16:26,352 --> 00:16:27,945
- Oh, boy.
- Nygma.

293
00:16:29,455 --> 00:16:30,684
MAYOR JAMES: This is bad.

294
00:16:44,370 --> 00:16:47,067
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

295
00:16:53,212 --> 00:16:54,840
Yeah, I think I'll pass.

296
00:16:55,548 --> 00:16:56,868
COBBLEPOT: You
cannot be serious.

297
00:16:56,949 --> 00:16:59,783
I've seen mass graves
more inviting than this place.

298
00:17:01,087 --> 00:17:03,386
Strange messed
me up pretty good.

299
00:17:03,556 --> 00:17:06,424
He convinced me I was
some sort of goddess.

300
00:17:06,592 --> 00:17:08,493
And it took me a
long time to get over it.

301
00:17:08,728 --> 00:17:11,220
Now, this place might be
bad, but Gotham is worse.

302
00:17:11,464 --> 00:17:13,626
Hey, freak. You're
on company time.

303
00:17:14,367 --> 00:17:15,562
Get back to work.

304
00:17:17,904 --> 00:17:19,270
IVY: You don't
have to take that.

305
00:17:19,906 --> 00:17:22,239
- You should totally kick his ass.
- Yeah.

306
00:17:22,408 --> 00:17:23,603
But he's my boss.

307
00:17:24,343 --> 00:17:27,108
Bridgit, there is nothing
wrong with being a freak.

308
00:17:28,848 --> 00:17:31,181
I'm a freak. So is Penguin.

309
00:17:32,184 --> 00:17:33,208
You belong with us.

310
00:17:35,755 --> 00:17:37,587
We've met before, haven't we?

311
00:17:38,257 --> 00:17:41,091
Yeah. I'm Ivy
Pepper. Selina's friend.

312
00:17:42,461 --> 00:17:45,124
Oh, I know. I ran into
one of Strange's puppies.

313
00:17:45,298 --> 00:17:48,200
Kind of had a growth spurt. Though,
to be honest, I'm not complaining.

314
00:17:49,602 --> 00:17:50,695
Ivy.

315
00:17:51,437 --> 00:17:54,066
- And you're part of this?
- Yeah.

316
00:17:54,941 --> 00:17:56,273
It's almost like we're a family.

317
00:17:57,443 --> 00:17:59,207
You don't have to
be alone anymore.

318
00:18:01,647 --> 00:18:03,775
I could kill your boss
just to sweeten the deal.

319
00:18:06,886 --> 00:18:07,910
Nah.

320
00:18:12,491 --> 00:18:15,120
- Hey, you. I quit.
- (GROANS)

321
00:18:16,062 --> 00:18:17,997
(MAN SCREAMING)

322
00:18:25,071 --> 00:18:26,972
Thank you for
letting me come in.

323
00:18:27,873 --> 00:18:29,398
The nosebleeds
are getting worse.

324
00:18:29,575 --> 00:18:31,510
You did the right
thing coming here.

325
00:18:31,911 --> 00:18:33,903
- What did you tell Alfred?
- Nothing.

326
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,272
I said I was tired, then
snuck out of my room.

327
00:18:43,923 --> 00:18:45,357
I'm dying, aren't I?

328
00:18:45,758 --> 00:18:46,758
Yes.

329
00:18:47,560 --> 00:18:48,584
I'm sorry.

330
00:18:48,995 --> 00:18:51,794
The process that brought
you into this world was flawed.

331
00:18:53,265 --> 00:18:55,063
Will I die before Bruce returns?

332
00:18:55,234 --> 00:18:58,295
No. Bruce Wayne will be back
in Gotham well before then.

333
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:03,500
I know we've asked a lot of you.

334
00:19:04,777 --> 00:19:07,440
After Indian Hill, I didn't know
what to do or where to go.

335
00:19:09,515 --> 00:19:11,143
You gave me a purpose.

336
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:14,682
That's more than
most people can say.

337
00:19:14,854 --> 00:19:17,153
I'm glad you see it that way.

338
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,558
When Bruce returns,

339
00:19:22,862 --> 00:19:24,797
people are going
to die, aren't they?

340
00:19:25,498 --> 00:19:26,498
A lot of people.

341
00:19:26,699 --> 00:19:29,760
You haven't gotten attached
to anyone, have you?

342
00:19:30,369 --> 00:19:32,099
<i>Alfred, perhaps?</i>

343
00:19:32,571 --> 00:19:34,597
<i>- You've spoken fondly of him.</i>
- No.

344
00:19:36,609 --> 00:19:38,009
I just want to know.

345
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:41,837
The number is immaterial.

346
00:19:43,249 --> 00:19:46,242
What matters is that
Gotham must fall.

347
00:19:46,752 --> 00:19:49,620
And because of
your sacrifice, it will.

348
00:19:51,891 --> 00:19:53,519
Can we count on you?

349
00:19:55,227 --> 00:19:56,227
Yes.

350
00:19:58,831 --> 00:20:01,096
His BP's dropping. We
need to stabilize him.

351
00:20:01,267 --> 00:20:04,760
I want this ER secured, badge
access only. No one gets in

352
00:20:04,937 --> 00:20:06,737
- unless they're sick or dying.
- WOMAN: 10-4.

353
00:20:06,806 --> 00:20:09,251
Nygma knows this is the closest
hospital to the Mayor's Office.

354
00:20:09,275 --> 00:20:10,395
We brought him right to him.

355
00:20:10,476 --> 00:20:12,968
Great. Let him show his face.
I got unis all over the place.

356
00:20:13,145 --> 00:20:14,773
What are we missing, Harvey?

357
00:20:14,947 --> 00:20:17,192
What could Aubrey James know
that's so important to Nygma?

358
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,811
ED: (OVER PA) <i>Paging
Detective James Gordon.</i>

359
00:20:19,985 --> 00:20:21,613
<i>Paging Detective James Gordon.</i>

360
00:20:21,787 --> 00:20:24,232
- Where's that coming from?
- Communications room. Second floor.

361
00:20:24,256 --> 00:20:25,256
It's a trap.

362
00:20:26,092 --> 00:20:28,036
- WOMAN: (OVER PA) <i>Please, don't kill me!</i>
- (GUNSHOTS)

363
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:29,060
Stay here.

364
00:20:30,529 --> 00:20:33,089
ED: <i>So, Jimbo. Now
you must be wondering</i>

365
00:20:33,265 --> 00:20:36,099
<i>what I want from that
ding-dong Aubrey James.</i>

366
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:41,072
<i>Well, turns out, he
has answers to a riddle.</i>

367
00:20:41,407 --> 00:20:44,536
<i>One that you put into motion when
you sent Barbara down to Dock 9C.</i>

368
00:20:45,010 --> 00:20:48,640
<i>The question being,
who runs Gotham?</i>

369
00:20:50,449 --> 00:20:51,974
I gotta get out of here.

370
00:20:52,151 --> 00:20:54,620
No, Mr. Mayor, you're in
no condition to go anywhere.

371
00:20:54,787 --> 00:20:56,688
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

372
00:20:57,423 --> 00:20:59,722
- Jim, tell me you got him.
- He wasn't there.

373
00:21:00,292 --> 00:21:02,784
But the secret he's
after, it's The Court.

374
00:21:03,129 --> 00:21:04,995
(INDISTINCT CHATTER)

375
00:21:07,133 --> 00:21:08,977
<i>- You better get back here, quick.</i>
- What is it?

376
00:21:09,001 --> 00:21:10,321
There was some
kind of explosion.

377
00:21:10,469 --> 00:21:12,665
A lot of victims. I
got a bad feeling.

378
00:21:12,838 --> 00:21:14,739
It's him. Don't leave
the Mayor's side.

379
00:21:15,741 --> 00:21:17,519
- Authorized personnel only.
- To hell with that.

380
00:21:17,543 --> 00:21:18,806
My friends got blown up.

381
00:21:19,011 --> 00:21:21,173
(MEN GRUNTING)

382
00:21:21,747 --> 00:21:23,716
(OBJECTS CLATTERING)

383
00:21:30,322 --> 00:21:31,346
Hello, Aubrey.

384
00:21:31,924 --> 00:21:32,983
(MEN GRUNTING)

385
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:55,106
We got company.

386
00:21:55,347 --> 00:21:56,440
Where is she?

387
00:21:57,416 --> 00:21:58,416
Not here.

388
00:21:58,584 --> 00:22:00,610
I know she and Nygma
kidnapped Mayor James.

389
00:22:00,986 --> 00:22:03,979
Nygma mentioned Dock 9C,
and she's the only one I told.

390
00:22:04,456 --> 00:22:05,685
Nygma's got a big mouth.

391
00:22:05,891 --> 00:22:07,571
Wait, wait, wait. Let
me get this straight.

392
00:22:07,726 --> 00:22:10,457
You mean this whole stupid
riddle thing with Nygma is real?

393
00:22:11,497 --> 00:22:13,693
What? He clearly
knows everything already.

394
00:22:15,534 --> 00:22:19,232
I heard a rumor he hurt
you pretty bad a while back.

395
00:22:19,505 --> 00:22:21,838
Both of you. Surprised
you're defending him.

396
00:22:22,341 --> 00:22:24,071
Listen, you tell
me where they are.

397
00:22:24,476 --> 00:22:25,944
I'll take Nygma down,

398
00:22:26,579 --> 00:22:28,070
but I'll get Barbara
a free pass.

399
00:22:33,519 --> 00:22:35,181
It's true. I hate him.

400
00:22:36,655 --> 00:22:37,953
But I don't know where they are.

401
00:22:38,858 --> 00:22:40,622
(CELL PHONE RINGING)

402
00:22:42,161 --> 00:22:43,356
JIM: <i>Harvey.</i>

403
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,824
Okay, I'll be right there.

404
00:22:46,599 --> 00:22:47,828
Nygma sent another riddle.

405
00:22:48,467 --> 00:22:50,187
<i>Never should have
brought Barbara into this.</i>

406
00:22:50,269 --> 00:22:52,431
You better hope
I get to her first.

407
00:22:53,906 --> 00:22:55,568
You should've
given that freak up.

408
00:22:56,242 --> 00:22:57,938
No one wants Nygma
dead more than me,

409
00:22:59,178 --> 00:23:00,669
but I can't betray Barbara.

410
00:23:01,146 --> 00:23:02,170
Yeah.

411
00:23:02,414 --> 00:23:04,679
Cause she's always got
your best interest at heart.

412
00:23:09,255 --> 00:23:12,282
Listen, you're in way
over your head on this one.

413
00:23:12,892 --> 00:23:14,532
You don't want to
mess with these people.

414
00:23:14,627 --> 00:23:16,323
You see, everything that you say

415
00:23:16,795 --> 00:23:20,562
just makes me more
intrigued and determined.

416
00:23:21,667 --> 00:23:24,967
I will be the one
who unmasks them.

417
00:23:25,271 --> 00:23:26,351
MAYOR JAMES: <i>You're insane.</i>

418
00:23:27,673 --> 00:23:30,006
Remember me, Aubrey?

419
00:23:31,076 --> 00:23:32,408
I know that voice.

420
00:23:32,978 --> 00:23:34,446
(WHISPERS) I'm so glad.

421
00:23:35,481 --> 00:23:39,646
I thought maybe it got muffled
what with that box on your head.

422
00:23:40,085 --> 00:23:41,085
(GIGGLES)

423
00:23:41,353 --> 00:23:44,380
That was fun. We should do
that again for old times' sake.

424
00:23:45,357 --> 00:23:46,985
You don't get it, do you?

425
00:23:47,626 --> 00:23:50,653
These people, they're like God.
They see and hear everything.

426
00:23:50,829 --> 00:23:52,297
They'll know I talked.

427
00:23:52,498 --> 00:23:54,228
(GASPS) Then it's the box.

428
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:56,040
(STAMMERS) No.
Please, anything but that.

429
00:24:00,940 --> 00:24:02,932
They call themselves The Court.

430
00:24:04,576 --> 00:24:05,576
And?

431
00:24:06,745 --> 00:24:09,715
That's all I know. I've
never met these people.

432
00:24:09,882 --> 00:24:11,748
I just did what they
asked me to, I swear.

433
00:24:12,618 --> 00:24:14,951
(CLAPPING)

434
00:24:15,454 --> 00:24:17,616
Very good. Thank you, Mr. Mayor.

435
00:24:18,090 --> 00:24:19,615
You've been very helpful.

436
00:24:21,260 --> 00:24:22,284
Helpful?

437
00:24:22,795 --> 00:24:24,286
All he gave us was "The Court."

438
00:24:24,663 --> 00:24:27,223
He gave us tangible
evidence of their existence.

439
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:29,434
Now they'll know
I'm not bluffing.

440
00:24:30,369 --> 00:24:31,449
What are you talking about?

441
00:24:31,570 --> 00:24:34,904
I'm going to force The
Court to reveal themselves.

442
00:24:36,208 --> 00:24:38,905
What is the one thing that every
secret organization is afraid of?

443
00:24:39,511 --> 00:24:40,740
Being exposed.

444
00:24:42,014 --> 00:24:43,107
Bingo.

445
00:24:45,584 --> 00:24:47,678
Finally. Did you
bring what I asked for?

446
00:24:54,193 --> 00:24:55,753
It's time to get The
Court's attention.

447
00:24:58,597 --> 00:24:59,597
Baby.

448
00:25:00,499 --> 00:25:02,627
Gordon came to the
club. He knows everything.

449
00:25:04,403 --> 00:25:06,497
You should've never
gotten Nygma involved.

450
00:25:18,951 --> 00:25:21,420
- I boosted the premium stuff, Otto.
- (MEOWING)

451
00:25:23,889 --> 00:25:25,414
You're welcome.

452
00:25:27,960 --> 00:25:29,053
BRUCE: Hello, Selina.

453
00:25:31,430 --> 00:25:33,023
What the hell are
you doing here?

454
00:25:33,665 --> 00:25:35,031
I wanted to see you.

455
00:25:36,035 --> 00:25:37,035
I missed you.

456
00:25:37,403 --> 00:25:39,804
Did you fall on your head?
I told you to stay away.

457
00:25:40,239 --> 00:25:41,263
You did?

458
00:25:42,341 --> 00:25:43,400
I forgot.

459
00:25:44,977 --> 00:25:46,468
Why are you acting so weird?

460
00:25:48,247 --> 00:25:51,115
(STAMMERS) I'm sorry. I
didn't sleep well last night.

461
00:25:51,417 --> 00:25:52,885
Mmm-hmm.

462
00:25:53,919 --> 00:25:55,547
Well, I just came
to feed my cat.

463
00:25:55,721 --> 00:25:57,383
So if you're not
gonna leave, I am.

464
00:25:57,556 --> 00:26:00,287
- I promised myself I'd stay away.
- (SIGHS)

465
00:26:00,659 --> 00:26:02,321
That it would be safer that way.

466
00:26:03,062 --> 00:26:04,086
But things have changed.

467
00:26:04,430 --> 00:26:05,796
What are you talking about?

468
00:26:06,732 --> 00:26:07,852
You know what? I don't care.

469
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,798
Just don't be here
when I get back.

470
00:26:10,002 --> 00:26:11,163
Selina, wait.

471
00:26:16,075 --> 00:26:17,338
I'm not Bruce.

472
00:26:22,147 --> 00:26:24,514
- DR. THOMPKINS: Jim.
- Lee, now's not a good time.

473
00:26:24,683 --> 00:26:26,174
DR. THOMPKINS:
Your uncle's autopsy.

474
00:26:26,351 --> 00:26:28,718
Ballistics came back
negative. No match.

475
00:26:28,954 --> 00:26:32,083
But there were microscopic tears
along the entry wound made postmortem.

476
00:26:33,292 --> 00:26:34,351
What are you saying?

477
00:26:34,626 --> 00:26:36,959
Someone removed the
bullet that killed your uncle

478
00:26:37,129 --> 00:26:38,722
and replaced it
with another one.

479
00:26:38,897 --> 00:26:40,661
It's an old mob trick
to cover up a murder.

480
00:26:40,833 --> 00:26:42,893
- You're reaching, Lee.
- I don't think so.

481
00:26:43,068 --> 00:26:44,468
And I think you
know what happened.

482
00:26:46,105 --> 00:26:49,007
Listen to me, you need to drop
this. You could get yourself hurt.

483
00:26:49,174 --> 00:26:51,234
You think I care
what happens to me?

484
00:26:51,510 --> 00:26:54,969
I am sick of watching you destroy
people's lives and get away with it.

485
00:26:55,147 --> 00:26:56,877
When I find out what you did,

486
00:26:57,049 --> 00:26:59,678
I'm going to make sure you pay
for it. And I'm going to enjoy it.

487
00:27:00,085 --> 00:27:01,085
Jim, hey.

488
00:27:01,887 --> 00:27:03,116
(KNOCKING ON DOOR)

489
00:27:09,928 --> 00:27:10,928
Where's the riddle?

490
00:27:11,163 --> 00:27:14,463
Me and Lucius took a crack at it,
but maybe you'll have better luck.

491
00:27:14,933 --> 00:27:17,164
"You can see me, but
you cannot touch me.

492
00:27:18,403 --> 00:27:20,599
"With the flick of a
switch, I enter your home,

493
00:27:21,373 --> 00:27:23,171
"with another, I
leave you alone.

494
00:27:24,376 --> 00:27:27,005
- "Where am I?"
- He's taunting us. If he kills James,

495
00:27:27,179 --> 00:27:30,411
the press is gonna hand us
our asses on the 6:00 news.

496
00:27:31,016 --> 00:27:32,040
Harvey, you're a genius.

497
00:27:32,484 --> 00:27:34,043
Yeah, tell me
something I don't know.

498
00:27:36,088 --> 00:27:39,786
<i>I have a question. What
is this mysterious Court</i>

499
00:27:41,293 --> 00:27:43,853
<i>that controls the levers
of power here in Gotham?</i>

500
00:27:44,029 --> 00:27:45,520
Alvarez, go to Channel 7!

501
00:27:45,697 --> 00:27:47,495
Find out where Nygma's
broadcasting from.

502
00:27:47,666 --> 00:27:51,933
<i>Our dear Mayor's
head be blown to bits</i>

503
00:27:52,538 --> 00:27:54,819
<i>- in order to keep their anonymity.</i>
- (CELL PHONE RINGING)

504
00:27:55,007 --> 00:27:57,101
(ED LAUGHING)

505
00:28:00,078 --> 00:28:02,206
- KATHRYN: <i>Are you watching the television?</i>
- I am.

506
00:28:02,514 --> 00:28:05,143
The Court cannot be exposed.

507
00:28:06,518 --> 00:28:10,148
We would clean this up on our own,
but there are too many eyes watching.

508
00:28:10,556 --> 00:28:14,652
<i>However, this does afford
us an opportunity, James.</i>

509
00:28:14,826 --> 00:28:15,826
To prove my loyalty.

510
00:28:17,663 --> 00:28:20,030
You want me to find
Nygma and bring him to you?

511
00:28:20,599 --> 00:28:23,831
I understand this puts
you in a difficult position.

512
00:28:24,503 --> 00:28:26,768
He's a cop killer.
He belongs in prison.

513
00:28:26,939 --> 00:28:29,602
KATHRYN: <i>If you decline,
this conversation will be our last.</i>

514
00:28:29,775 --> 00:28:31,175
The choice is yours.

515
00:28:32,778 --> 00:28:34,144
That was The Court.

516
00:28:34,880 --> 00:28:37,161
- If I hand him over, I'm in.
- They'll probably kill him.

517
00:28:37,282 --> 00:28:40,275
If I don't, we'll never stop
them from destroying the city.

518
00:28:41,887 --> 00:28:43,327
<i>I know what you're
thinking, Aubrey.</i>

519
00:28:43,355 --> 00:28:46,917
That the police are gonna
somehow find you, rescue you.

520
00:28:47,759 --> 00:28:50,786
But I gave the GCPD
every chance to save you.

521
00:28:51,163 --> 00:28:54,861
<i>But they're no match
for me!</i> (LAUGHING)

522
00:28:57,169 --> 00:28:58,467
We're both dead men.

523
00:28:59,471 --> 00:29:01,099
You don't get it, do you?

524
00:29:02,507 --> 00:29:04,147
The Court's isn't
gonna bargain with you.

525
00:29:04,176 --> 00:29:05,176
(CELL PHONE RINGS)

526
00:29:05,811 --> 00:29:07,439
You underestimate me, Mr. James.

527
00:29:12,184 --> 00:29:13,880
- Hello.
- Nygma.

528
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:19,186
Jim. I'm so sorry. We can't
be clogging up the lines.

529
00:29:19,358 --> 00:29:21,156
I'm actually expecting
an important call.

530
00:29:21,326 --> 00:29:23,124
JIM: <i>You wanna know
who runs Gotham?</i>

531
00:29:23,695 --> 00:29:26,358
I have the answer.
Come by the GCPD.

532
00:29:26,965 --> 00:29:27,965
I'll tell it to you.

533
00:29:28,200 --> 00:29:30,135
Hmm. Yeah, I think
I'll pass on that.

534
00:29:30,302 --> 00:29:31,622
<i>Then you'll never
know the truth.</i>

535
00:29:32,004 --> 00:29:33,734
You think I told Barbara
everything I know?

536
00:29:35,040 --> 00:29:38,238
You always were
clever, Jim. I respect that.

537
00:29:38,977 --> 00:29:40,468
<i>Empty out the GCPD.</i>

538
00:29:40,946 --> 00:29:44,542
<i>I want it to just be
you and me. Alone.</i>

539
00:29:44,950 --> 00:29:48,546
<i>Well, and this idiot with
the bomb around his neck.</i>

540
00:29:51,556 --> 00:29:52,556
(GRUNTS)

541
00:29:56,261 --> 00:29:57,661
BULLOCK: You think he'll show?

542
00:29:58,297 --> 00:30:00,493
JIM: The thing that drives
Nygma is also his weakness.

543
00:30:00,666 --> 00:30:01,690
He'll be here.

544
00:30:01,900 --> 00:30:03,540
You sound like every
man, woman and child

545
00:30:03,568 --> 00:30:05,730
in Gotham isn't depending
on you to succeed.

546
00:30:05,904 --> 00:30:07,236
Yeah, no pressure.

547
00:30:10,475 --> 00:30:12,068
- Good luck, pal.
- Thanks.

548
00:30:18,884 --> 00:30:19,908
Where's Ed?

549
00:30:20,085 --> 00:30:22,247
That lunatic dropped
me off, sent me in alone.

550
00:30:22,421 --> 00:30:24,822
- Get the bomb squad in here.
- Sit down and shut up.

551
00:30:27,659 --> 00:30:30,493
Ed. It's just the
two of us in here.

552
00:30:32,998 --> 00:30:35,279
ED: Just wanted to make
sure I wasn't walking into a trap.

553
00:30:36,768 --> 00:30:38,293
Nah, uh-uh.

554
00:30:39,471 --> 00:30:40,471
Sit down, Aubrey.

555
00:30:44,276 --> 00:30:46,276
You said you had the
answer I was looking for, Jim.

556
00:30:46,478 --> 00:30:49,243
It would be incredibly
disappointing if this was all a ruse.

557
00:30:49,414 --> 00:30:50,677
More so for Mayor James.

558
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,136
Just tell him what he wants.

559
00:30:52,951 --> 00:30:53,951
He talks too much.

560
00:30:54,252 --> 00:30:55,379
(LAUGHS)

561
00:30:55,654 --> 00:30:57,614
You should probably just
go ahead and blow him up.

562
00:30:57,756 --> 00:30:59,436
MAYOR JAMES: <i>I'll
have your badge, Gordon.</i>

563
00:31:01,193 --> 00:31:02,354
I'm not bluffing, Jim.

564
00:31:02,761 --> 00:31:03,888
Neither am I.

565
00:31:04,896 --> 00:31:06,407
<i>What's the blast
radius on that thing?</i>

566
00:31:06,431 --> 00:31:09,492
Am I good here? Or should
I duck behind the desk?

567
00:31:09,668 --> 00:31:11,660
I want the answer, Jim!

568
00:31:15,974 --> 00:31:20,002
I kill him, I still walk out of
here with you as my hostage.

569
00:31:23,482 --> 00:31:25,474
- (CLICKS)
- No. No!

570
00:31:27,052 --> 00:31:28,092
- No!
- (DETONATOR BEEPING)

571
00:31:28,220 --> 00:31:29,848
(RADIO FREQUENCY BUZZING)

572
00:31:30,455 --> 00:31:31,650
Oh, come on.

573
00:31:33,325 --> 00:31:35,419
There's a radio frequency
jamming the signal

574
00:31:35,594 --> 00:31:36,871
between the detonator
and the bomb.

575
00:31:36,895 --> 00:31:38,659
- How?
- Tabitha.

576
00:31:39,231 --> 00:31:40,995
She's holds quite the
grudge against you.

577
00:31:41,166 --> 00:31:44,000
She called me. Told me
how to disarm the bomb.

578
00:31:44,569 --> 00:31:45,901
(CHUCKLES)

579
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:48,886
I'll admit, I didn't
see this coming.

580
00:31:50,041 --> 00:31:51,976
But that doesn't
change anything.

581
00:31:52,944 --> 00:31:57,609
I want to know who The Court is.

582
00:31:59,551 --> 00:32:00,551
Or Aubrey dies.

583
00:32:03,088 --> 00:32:04,088
Don't.

584
00:32:07,659 --> 00:32:09,093
You wanna know who runs Gotham?

585
00:32:10,128 --> 00:32:11,858
Then let Mayor James go.

586
00:32:12,697 --> 00:32:13,858
Take a ride with me.

587
00:32:14,399 --> 00:32:15,628
But if you pull that trigger,

588
00:32:15,834 --> 00:32:17,674
you'll never get the
answer you're looking for.

589
00:32:19,871 --> 00:32:21,669
You fool me once, Jim.

590
00:32:22,073 --> 00:32:23,735
(CLICKS TONGUE) Shame on you.

591
00:32:24,876 --> 00:32:26,538
You fool me twice!

592
00:32:28,180 --> 00:32:29,580
Well, that's just
not gonna happen.

593
00:32:29,614 --> 00:32:31,207
<i>Then the riddle
will go unsolved.</i>

594
00:32:39,057 --> 00:32:40,081
Fine.

595
00:32:47,399 --> 00:32:48,399
Let's go.

596
00:32:49,301 --> 00:32:51,202
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

597
00:32:51,536 --> 00:32:52,970
SELINA: <i>Let me
get this straight.</i>

598
00:32:53,405 --> 00:32:57,604
So, this limo pulls up,
literally out of nowhere,

599
00:32:57,909 --> 00:33:00,435
and this creepy
lady tells you to get in

600
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:03,945
because "you could
be so much more."

601
00:33:04,616 --> 00:33:05,811
And you did?

602
00:33:06,384 --> 00:33:07,875
I had nowhere else to go.

603
00:33:08,119 --> 00:33:09,839
So, where have you
been the last few months?

604
00:33:09,921 --> 00:33:10,921
It's not important.

605
00:33:11,490 --> 00:33:13,130
What matters is you
need to leave Gotham.

606
00:33:13,191 --> 00:33:14,523
- Right away.
- Why?

607
00:33:15,794 --> 00:33:17,114
Because the city
has been judged.

608
00:33:17,262 --> 00:33:18,542
And something bad is going to...

609
00:33:18,597 --> 00:33:20,088
(SCOFFS) Judged by who?

610
00:33:22,767 --> 00:33:24,235
The people who took you?

611
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:27,539
Wait a minute. Your
clothes, your hair.

612
00:33:28,473 --> 00:33:29,473
<i>The way you talk.</i>

613
00:33:33,111 --> 00:33:34,135
Where is Bruce?

614
00:33:34,513 --> 00:33:36,675
- Selina...
- What did you do to him?

615
00:33:36,848 --> 00:33:38,339
He's fine. He's not in Gotham,

616
00:33:38,950 --> 00:33:40,361
but nothing bad is
going to happen to him.

617
00:33:40,385 --> 00:33:42,354
- Then where is he?
- It doesn't matter.

618
00:33:42,554 --> 00:33:44,921
You just have to trust me. You
need to leave Gotham today.

619
00:33:45,190 --> 00:33:46,419
Trust you?

620
00:33:48,326 --> 00:33:51,091
- (SCOFFS) I don't even know you.
- Where are you going?

621
00:33:52,197 --> 00:33:53,426
- To tell Alfred.
- Selina...

622
00:33:53,632 --> 00:33:55,066
Now, let me go.

623
00:33:55,267 --> 00:33:56,467
Selina, you can't tell anyone.

624
00:33:56,601 --> 00:33:57,961
Then why the hell
did you tell me?

625
00:34:01,139 --> 00:34:02,232
Because I care about you.

626
00:34:03,308 --> 00:34:06,301
And if there's one person I
want to save, I want it to be you.

627
00:34:07,479 --> 00:34:08,879
(CHUCKLES)

628
00:34:09,681 --> 00:34:12,947
That's the difference
between you and Bruce Wayne.

629
00:34:15,220 --> 00:34:17,052
He would try and save everyone.

630
00:34:18,957 --> 00:34:21,358
You can pretend all you want.

631
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:24,325
But you will never be him.

632
00:34:24,963 --> 00:34:27,660
You're nothing. You're
not even a real person.

633
00:34:29,568 --> 00:34:30,627
You don't matter.

634
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,072
You're wrong about me.

635
00:34:36,908 --> 00:34:38,069
I do matter.

636
00:34:39,311 --> 00:34:41,473
- And I won't let you tell Alfred.
- Oh, yeah?

637
00:34:43,048 --> 00:34:44,048
How are you gonna stop...

638
00:34:44,249 --> 00:34:45,547
(SELINA SCREAMING)

639
00:35:19,651 --> 00:35:23,486
Remember the night you
came over to Lee's for dinner?

640
00:35:25,957 --> 00:35:27,721
It feels like a lifetime ago.

641
00:35:28,193 --> 00:35:29,923
Leslie made fondue.

642
00:35:31,096 --> 00:35:32,655
The wine was a Bordeaux.

643
00:35:34,265 --> 00:35:36,234
Well aged. Smooth tannins.

644
00:35:38,503 --> 00:35:41,905
Miss Kringle wore a
black dress with pink trim.

645
00:35:43,308 --> 00:35:45,140
I tried like hell
to get out of it.

646
00:35:45,577 --> 00:35:46,943
(ED CHUCKLES)

647
00:35:47,345 --> 00:35:48,711
Lee insisted.

648
00:35:49,714 --> 00:35:51,774
The truth is, I had a good time.

649
00:35:55,286 --> 00:35:56,686
I considered you a friend.

650
00:35:59,424 --> 00:36:00,756
I can sneak up on you

651
00:36:00,959 --> 00:36:03,190
or be right in front of you
without you even knowing.

652
00:36:03,395 --> 00:36:05,125
But when I reveal myself,

653
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:08,060
you will never be the same.

654
00:36:08,233 --> 00:36:09,701
- What am I?
- I don't care, Ed.

655
00:36:09,868 --> 00:36:11,029
Betrayal.

656
00:36:13,204 --> 00:36:14,729
That's how every
friendship ends.

657
00:36:17,108 --> 00:36:18,974
So, what good are
friends anyway?

658
00:36:33,191 --> 00:36:34,284
Who are they?

659
00:36:34,492 --> 00:36:36,120
The answer to your question.

660
00:36:55,346 --> 00:36:56,974
Hello, Mr. Nygma.

661
00:36:57,348 --> 00:36:59,112
I hear you've been
asking about us.

662
00:36:59,284 --> 00:37:00,809
How do I know you're real?

663
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:04,880
Isn't that the point
of a good mystery?

664
00:37:05,523 --> 00:37:08,687
You're never quite sure
what to believe until the end.

665
00:37:09,060 --> 00:37:10,460
Gordon could've
put you up to this.

666
00:37:10,528 --> 00:37:15,057
I assure you, Detective Gordon
had to be convinced to bring you here.

667
00:37:16,167 --> 00:37:18,033
But let me put it like this.

668
00:37:18,636 --> 00:37:20,434
That question Professor Strange

669
00:37:20,605 --> 00:37:24,736
had you ask Bruce Wayne and
Lucius Fox last year at Indian Hill,

670
00:37:25,310 --> 00:37:27,745
the one that has tortured you,

671
00:37:28,947 --> 00:37:31,610
the one you'll never
be able to answer...

672
00:37:31,783 --> 00:37:33,376
That answer is with me.

673
00:37:34,185 --> 00:37:35,744
(EXHALES DEEPLY)

674
00:37:37,756 --> 00:37:38,951
What now?

675
00:37:39,124 --> 00:37:40,285
<i>Get in.</i>

676
00:37:40,458 --> 00:37:42,950
And all your questions
will be answered.

677
00:37:44,229 --> 00:37:45,720
You won't be needing the gun.

678
00:38:08,453 --> 00:38:09,453
(THUNDER RUMBLING)

679
00:38:09,721 --> 00:38:12,520
You've made us proud,
Detective Gordon.

680
00:38:12,757 --> 00:38:14,248
What are you
going to do with him?

681
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:18,122
A man with Nygma's intellect
could be quite useful to us.

682
00:38:18,463 --> 00:38:20,591
<i>I'm sure we'll find
something for him to do.</i>

683
00:38:22,667 --> 00:38:23,896
We'll be in touch.

684
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:32,069
(ALTERNATIVE ROCK PLAYING)

685
00:38:46,291 --> 00:38:48,283
Good evening, Ms. Kean.
May I offer you a drink?

686
00:38:48,893 --> 00:38:50,191
(BOTTLE SHATTERS)

687
00:38:50,628 --> 00:38:51,687
Something went wrong.

688
00:38:51,863 --> 00:38:52,863
Gordon took down Nygma

689
00:38:53,031 --> 00:38:55,330
before he could find out
the truth about The Court.

690
00:38:56,034 --> 00:38:58,114
Probably 'cause I told Gordon
how to disarm the bomb.

691
00:38:58,870 --> 00:38:59,997
What?

692
00:39:00,772 --> 00:39:01,772
Why?

693
00:39:01,940 --> 00:39:03,374
You promised that when Nygma

694
00:39:03,541 --> 00:39:05,581
handed over the underworld,
I would get to kill him.

695
00:39:07,812 --> 00:39:09,542
Sealed it with a kiss, remember?

696
00:39:11,416 --> 00:39:12,543
Don't you get it?

697
00:39:13,384 --> 00:39:15,717
As long as The
Court is out there,

698
00:39:15,887 --> 00:39:18,721
I'll never be in control!

699
00:39:21,292 --> 00:39:23,454
Don't you mean, "We'll
never be in control"?

700
00:39:32,203 --> 00:39:34,229
Seen it a thousand times.

701
00:39:35,139 --> 00:39:37,165
Ambition. Power.

702
00:39:38,009 --> 00:39:39,443
People can't help themselves.

703
00:39:40,178 --> 00:39:41,703
She's changed, baby.

704
00:39:42,814 --> 00:39:44,976
- When are you gonna see that?
- Shut up, Butch!

705
00:39:45,984 --> 00:39:47,179
Move!

706
00:39:49,621 --> 00:39:51,055
This is trouble.

707
00:39:57,328 --> 00:39:58,660
It's good to be home.

708
00:39:59,030 --> 00:40:02,125
FYI, I've been to Wayne
Manor. It's way cleaner.

709
00:40:03,167 --> 00:40:05,932
You never said anything
about Fries being a part of this.

710
00:40:06,471 --> 00:40:07,769
You're a little hot.

711
00:40:08,306 --> 00:40:09,386
Maybe you need to cool off.

712
00:40:10,008 --> 00:40:11,088
IVY: <i>Oh, come on, you guys.</i>

713
00:40:11,609 --> 00:40:13,339
We're on the same
team now, remember?

714
00:40:14,412 --> 00:40:15,505
A family?

715
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:17,409
(WEAPONS POWER DOWN)

716
00:40:19,217 --> 00:40:20,617
Keep him away from me.

717
00:40:27,859 --> 00:40:30,090
There's a question
mark on your face.

718
00:40:31,763 --> 00:40:33,425
You can sleep in the freezer.

719
00:40:33,932 --> 00:40:36,697
(TV PLAYING)

720
00:40:40,238 --> 00:40:41,706
Hey, Pengy. Check it out.

721
00:40:41,873 --> 00:40:44,502
Do not call me Pengy! My...

722
00:40:44,676 --> 00:40:47,703
<i>AKA Edward Nygma, was
apprehended by the GCPD</i>

723
00:40:47,879 --> 00:40:51,407
<i>this afternoon after kidnapping
interim Mayor Aubrey James.</i>

724
00:40:51,883 --> 00:40:53,563
<i>However, while en
route to Arkham Asylum...</i>

725
00:40:53,718 --> 00:40:54,718
Riddler.

726
00:40:54,919 --> 00:40:57,650
<i>He managed to escape police
custody and is now at large.</i>

727
00:40:57,855 --> 00:41:00,791
How long did he have
to think about that one?

728
00:41:07,899 --> 00:41:08,923
Rest up, everyone.

729
00:41:10,368 --> 00:41:13,338
Tomorrow is going
to be a busy day.

730
00:41:19,811 --> 00:41:22,508
(CAT MEOWING)

731
00:41:32,123 --> 00:41:33,955
(CONTINUES MEOWING)

732
00:42:15,466 --> 00:42:20,427
I'd like to introduce our
newest member, James Gordon.

733
00:42:33,918 --> 00:42:36,114
<i>Welcome to The Court of Owls.</i>

734
00:42:45,263 --> 00:42:47,255
(THEME MUSIC PLAYING)

735
00:43:20,331 --> 00:43:21,331
English -SDH
